  "answer": {
    "question": "Can Harborlight afford a sixth site?",
    "text": "The sources don't say whether Harborlight can afford a sixth site, because they don't show how the $1,610,000 FY2027 budget would be paid for.\nStaff ask the board to approve an FY2027 budget of $1,610,000. It would add a sixth site at the Eastgate branch library and two site coordinators [1]. For comparison, FY2026 operating expenses were $1,420,000 [2]. That year, foundation grants gave $640,000, individual donors gave $388,000 and the city contract paid $295,000 [2].\nOne sign of strain comes from the board notes. Reserves stand at 3.2 months of operating expenses, which is below the board's goal of 4 months [3].\nThe board planned to vote on the budget on October 21 [3]. The sources don't report how that vote went, and they show no funding plan for the new site.",
